            <ArticleTitle>Elderly patient with acute, left lower abdominal pain: perforated jejunal diverticulitis (2010:7b).</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>2541-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1007/s00330-010-1726-6</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>An elderly patient with acute, left, lower abdominal pain is described, for whom the diagnosis of perforated jejunal diverticulitis was established by computed tomography (CT). The presence of a jejunal segmental inflammatory process, with or without abscess or perforation, in the setting of jejunal diverticulosis, is very suggestive of jejunal diverticulitis.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
